nightsiege.guide.events.body:
From level 3 a siege brings an event 45 % of the time. It is never announced: you see it in the sky and on the monsters. During an event zombies, skeletons, creepers and spiders take on its look.

@minecraft:redstone_block|§cBlood moon§r: red moon and sky, 1.5× as many monsters, tougher and harder hitting.
@minecraft:golden_sword|§6Champion§r: a glowing golden leader. Once it falls, the rest of the wave deals 25 % less damage.
@minecraft:zombie_head|§eTheme wave§r: the whole night is a single kind of monster.
@minecraft:black_concrete|§5Solar eclipse§r: once the countdown is done, the sun goes dark at noon and the siege comes by day. The undead do not burn and phantoms join in. A horn warns shortly before.
@minecraft:cobweb|§7Fog night§r: you see only a few blocks, the monsters are silent, more spiders and creepers.
@minecraft:lightning_rod|§bThunder night§r: lightning strikes the attackers and charges creepers. Tesla coils hit 50 % harder. No natural lightning, nothing catches fire.
@minecraft:crying_obsidian|§4Nether rift§r: rifts open around the base and half the attackers come from the Nether. Ash falls from the sky.
@minecraft:powder_snow_bucket|§fFrost night§r: a blizzard, strays instead of skeletons. Anyone out in the open slows down and freezes (no damage). Leather armour keeps the cold out.

Events never change blocks. Like the blood moon, frost, rift and fog nights have a moon of their own.

## With shaders
Shader packs such as Complementary or Reverie draw sky, moon and fog themselves. Night Siege then lays the event colour, the event moon, the eclipse and the aurora over the picture as a layer of its own, so they still show. Monster textures and particles work with any shader.

nightsiege.guide.infernite.body:
Infernite is the tier after netherite.

## Getting it
@nightsiege:infernite_ore|Infernite Ore: in the Nether, as rare as ancient debris and always hidden. Needs a diamond pickaxe.
@nightsiege:infernite_scrap|Smelted: Infernite Scrap
@nightsiege:infernite_ingot|4 scrap + 1 netherite ingot = 1 infernite ingot

## Smithing template
@nightsiege:infernite_upgrade_smithing_template|You get one when your ult reaches its top rank. Copy it: template + 7 diamonds + 1 infernite block = 2 templates.

At the smithing table: template + netherite item + infernite ingot. Bow, crossbow, shield and mace are upgraded straight from the normal version.

## Class items
Every path has one infernite item. While you hold or wear the item of your path, your skills and ult work §ealways§r, not only in sieges. Every other infernite item is simply strong gear.

## Trying it in creative
In creative every class item lends you its path, fully levelled. §eSneak + R§r switches between paths on items with several.

nightsiege.guide.perks.body:
Set core fragments from dungeons into your siege core: fragment in hand, right-click the core (sneaking sets in the whole stack). Perks belong to everyone and work on every player within §e64 blocks§r of a core.

Stage 1 costs 1 fragment, stage 2 another 2, and so on. Stage V takes 15 fragments of one kind. The perk tab in the core window shows where you stand.

@nightsiege:core_fragment_vitality|§cVitality§r (easy ruins): +2 hearts per stage
@nightsiege:core_fragment_bulwark|§7Bulwark§r (outposts, castles): +1 armor and 5 % less damage per stage
@nightsiege:core_fragment_tides|§bTides§r (sea): Regeneration I, from stage III Regeneration II
@nightsiege:core_fragment_flame|§6Flame§r (Nether): +10 % damage per stage, from stage III fire resistance
@nightsiege:core_fragment_vigilance|§eVigilance§r (every guardian): −10 % ult cooldown and +10 % experience per stage

nightsiege.guide.traps.body:
Anyone can craft traps; only an engineer with the matching skill can set them. They only hit monsters, never players - by day as well. Every trap grows with its owner's tier.

## Cap per player
How many traps of one kind you may have at once rises with the tier.

@nightsiege:spike_trap|Spike Trap: damage + slow. 10-14. Recipe: 3 iron over 3 cobblestone (2×)
@nightsiege:snare_trap|Snare Trap: holds everything around. 4-6. 3 string, string-iron-string, 3 cobblestone (2×)
@nightsiege:blast_mine|Blast Mine: one explosion, no block damage. 6-10. Gunpowder, pressure plate, gunpowder over 3 cobblestone (2×)
@nightsiege:arrow_turret|Arrow Turret: shoots monsters, reload with arrows (right click). 2-6. Iron-dispenser-iron, iron-bow-iron, 3 cobblestone
@nightsiege:flame_trap|Flame Trap: sets alight. 3-5. Iron, fire charge, iron over 3 cobblestone (2×)
@nightsiege:poison_trap|Poison Trap: poison cloud. 3-7. Spider eye, fermented eye, spider eye over 3 cobblestone (2×)
@nightsiege:tesla_coil|Tesla Coil: chain lightning, no ammunition. 2-4. Copper, lightning rod, copper / iron, redstone block, iron / 3 cobblestone
